            "description": "## Accept Trip Request\n\nThis endpoint allows a driver to accept a specific trip identified by its unique trip ID. The request is sent via an HTTP POST method to the URL: `https://road-assist.test/api/v1/trips/{trip_id}/accept`, where `{trip_id}` is the ID of the trip being accepted.\n\n### Request Parameters\n\nThe request body must include the following parameter:\n\n- **driver_id** (string): The unique identifier of the driver accepting the trip. This parameter is required and should be provided in the form-data format.\n    \n\n### Response Structure\n\nUpon successful acceptance of the trip, the server will respond with a confirmation message and relevant trip details. The structure of the response typically includes:\n\n- **status**: Indicates the success or failure of the request.\n    \n- **message**: A descriptive message regarding the acceptance of the trip.\n    \n- **trip_details**: An object containing information about the trip, such as the destination, estimated time of arrival, and other relevant trip data.\n    \n\n### Example\n\n#### Request\n\n``` plaintext\nPOST /api/v1/trips/13/accept\nContent-Type: multipart/form-data\ndriver_id=12345\n\n ```\n\n#### Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"message\": \"Trip accepted successfully\",\n  \"trip_details\": {\n    \"destination\": \"123 Main St\",\n    \"eta\": \"15 minutes\"\n  }\n}\n\n ```\n\nEnsure that the `driver_id` is valid and corresponds to an existing driver in the system to avoid errors during the acceptance process."
          },
