            "description": "## Get Trip Details\n\nThis endpoint retrieves detailed information about a specific trip identified by its unique ID.\n\n### Request\n\n- **Method**: GET\n    \n- **URL**: `https://road-assist.test/api/v1/trips/{tripId}`\n    \n\n#### Path Parameters\n\n- `tripId` (required): The unique identifier for the trip. In this example, it is `1`.\n    \n\n### Response\n\nUpon a successful request, the server will respond with a JSON object containing the details of the trip. The structure of the response includes a `data` object with the following properties:\n\n- `id` (number): The unique identifier of the trip.\n    \n- `status` (string): The current status of the trip.\n    \n- `type` (string): The type of trip.\n    \n- `pickup` (object): An object containing:\n    \n    - `latitude` (number): The latitude of the pickup location.\n        \n    - `longitude` (number): The longitude of the pickup location.\n        \n- `created_at` (string): The timestamp of when the trip was created.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"type\": \"standard\",\n    \"pickup\": {\n      \"latitude\": 40.7128,\n      \"longitude\": -74.0060\n    },\n    \"created_at\": \"2023-10-01T09:00:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n\n ```\n\nThis endpoint is useful for retrieving comprehensive details about a specific trip, allowing users to track and manage their travel history effectively.\n\nThis endpoint retrieves detailed information about a specific trip identified by its unique ID.\n\n### Request\n\n- **Method**: GET\n    \n- **URL**: `https://road-assist.test/api/v1/trips/{tripId}`\n    \n\n#### Path Parameters\n\n- `tripId` (required): The unique identifier for the trip. In this example, it is `1`.\n    \n\n### Response\n\nUpon a successful request, the server will respond with a JSON object containing the details of the trip. The structure of the response typically includes:\n\n- `id`: The unique identifier of the trip.\n    \n- `destination`: The destination of the trip.\n    \n- `start_time`: The start time of the trip.\n    \n- `end_time`: The end time of the trip.\n    \n- `status`: The current status of the trip.\n    \n- `user`: Information about the user associated with the trip.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n   \"data\": {\n        \"id\": 1,\n        \"status\": \"started\",\n        \"type\": \"normal\",\n        \"pickup\": {\n            \"latitude\": 24.4539,\n            \"longitude\": 54.3773\n        },\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22 20:10:14\"\n    }\n\n ```\n\nThis endpoint is useful for retrieving comprehensive details about a specific trip, allowing users to track and manage their travel history effectively."
          },
